1396	//
1397	// REAL product-key top-k routing (restored): the query projection is split into
1398	// halves q_a / q_b; we score against product-key sub-codebooks A and B, take the
1399	// top-k of EACH (k = peer_topk, default 4), form the k×k Cartesian product of
1400	// candidate experts (expert = a_idx * nb + b_idx), softmax-weight them by the
1401	// summed sub-scores, run the per-element expert MLP for each of the k² selected
