**Current:**
```cpp
    // (3) Combine contexts (sum of fine + coarse), PEER routing + expert MLP.
    auto feat = csa_ctx + hca_ctx;  // [N, d_model]
    auto expert_sorted = detail::peer_expert_forward(
        feat, peer_query_Ws, prod_keys_A, prod_keys_B,
        expert_W1, expert_b1, expert_W2, expert_b2,
        N, d_model, num_experts, expert_hidden, expert_counts,
        /*peer_topk=*/peer_topk);  // [N] sorted ...
```

This is wrong **three ways** vs. the oracle `bilevel_forward_save:569-586`: (a) it **sums** `csa_ctx+hca_ctx` instead of **concatenating** them; (b) it omits `gru_new`, `g_sorted`, `s_sorted`; (c) width is 8, not 22. The PEER `query` projection weight expects width `peer_input_dim = 22`.

**Replacement (concept — see scope note):**
```cpp
    // (3) Build the real PEER input = cat(gru_new, csa_ctx, hca_ctx, g, s)
    //     all in SORTED order (csa/hca are sorted here; sort g,s by the same perm).
    auto g_sorted = grad.reshape({N}).to(torch::kFloat32).index_select(0, perm);
    auto s_sorted = sharpness.reshape({N}).to(torch::kFloat32).index_select(0, perm);
    auto gru_new  = /* run matrix GRU forward (W_z/W_r/W_h) — see scope note */;
    auto peer_input = torch::cat(
        {gru_new, csa_ctx, hca_ctx, g_sorted.unsqueeze(1), s_sorted.unsqueeze(1)}, 1);  // [N, 22]
    auto expert_sorted = detail::peer_expert_forward(
        peer_input, g_sorted, peer_query_Ws, prod_keys_A, prod_keys_B,
        expert_W1, expert_b1, expert_W2, expert_b2,
        N, d_model, num_experts, expert_hidden, expert_counts,
        /*peer_topk=*/peer_topk);
```

**Scope note (critical, and why this is the largest fix):** the fused forward currently has **no `gru_new`** — the matrix GRU is replaced by a per-element blend folded into `mu_state` with `gru_decay = beta1` (line 1690-1692; `gru_W*` args are `(void)`'d at 1688-1689). To make `peer_input` exactly oracle-faithful you must run the matrix GRU forward (`W_z/W_r/W_h`, the `xh`/`xrh`/`sigmoid`/`tanh` block) in `csa_hca_step_one`, using the template at `bilevel_forward_save:569-582`. That requires plumbing `gru_Wz/bz/Wr/br/Wh/bh` (already passed into `launch_csa_hca_step` at lines 1665-1666 but dropped before `csa_hca_step_one`) down into the function. This GRU reconstruction is a substantially larger change than the PEER patch itself.

